<!-- ===================== WHAT IT IS ===================== -->
<section class="sheet"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">// preflight briefing</p>
  <h2>One install. A whole operating discipline.</h2>
  <div class="trio">
    <article class="panel reveal">
      <span class="panel-ix">01</span>
      <h3>Layered context</h3>
      <p>Root + per-area <code>CLAUDE.md</code>, always-loaded rules (TDD, phase-matrix, git, LSP-first), and a hot-path lesson file. The agent boots with your conventions already loaded.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="panel reveal">
      <span class="panel-ix">02</span>
      <h3>Specialists, not a generalist</h3>
      <p>An orchestrator routes work to a backend/frontend engineer, a design-doc writer, a tech-lead reviewer — each with a scoped tool-belt and a cost-aware model tier.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="panel reveal">
      <span class="panel-ix">03</span>
      <h3>Gates that don't bend</h3>
      <p>Design-doc before code. Failing test first. A 6-gate post-delegation review before merge. A live mini-retro after every task. Discipline encoded as workflow.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- ===================== FLIGHT PATH (workflow) ===================== -->
<section class="sheet dark flightpath"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">// flight path</p>
  <h2>Every feature flies the same route: <span class="glow">idea → ship → retro</span></h2>
  <p class="lede">Each stage produces an artifact; the next can't start until the previous lands. The 6-gate review is the runway you can't skip.</p>

  <div class="route reveal">
    <div class="route-line"><span class="pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
    <ol class="stops">
      <li style="--s:0"><span class="dot"></span><b>/discover</b><small>interview → brief</small></li>
      <li style="--s:1"><span class="dot"></span><b>/promote</b><small>brief → backlog</small></li>
      <li style="--s:2"><span class="dot"></span><b>/next-task</b><small>pick + route</small></li>
      <li style="--s:3"><span class="dot"></span><b>design-doc</b><small>≥500-line zero-fix</small></li>
      <li style="--s:4"><span class="dot"></span><b>engineer</b><small>TDD: red → green</small></li>
      <li style="--s:5"><span class="dot gate"></span><b>6-gate review</b><small>inspect→…→smoke</small></li>
      <li style="--s:6"><span class="dot done"></span><b>mini-retro</b><small>capture learning</small></li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- 6-gate strip -->
  <div class="gates reveal">
    <p class="gates-h mono">// post-delegation review — no gate skipped, ever</p>
    <ol class="gatelights">
      <li style="--g:0"><i></i>Inspect diff</li>
      <li style="--g:1"><i></i>Build + Test</li>
      <li style="--g:2"><i></i>Boundary</li>
      <li style="--g:3"><i></i>Spec → Quality</li>
      <li style="--g:4"><i></i>Wiring</li>
      <li style="--g:5"><i></i>Integration smoke</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- ===================== MISSION PROFILES (use cases) ===================== -->
<section class="sheet soft missions"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">// mission profiles</p>
  <h2>What it looks like on a real task</h2>
  <p class="lede">Four common situations — and exactly how the control plane flies each one.</p>

  <div class="mgrid">
    <article class="mission reveal">
      <header><span class="mtag">01 · greenfield</span><h3>Build a new feature</h3></header>
      <p>You want a new endpoint. The orchestrator won't let code start without a design doc.</p>
      <ol class="flow">
        <li>/next-task picks it &amp; reads the <em>phase matrix</em> (type = feat)</li>
        <li>design-doc-writer (Opus) authors a zero-fix D-doc</li>
        <li>backend-engineer (Sonnet) writes the <strong>failing test first</strong></li>
        <li>6-gate review → mini-retro → ship</li>
      </ol>
    </article>

    <article class="mission reveal hot">
      <header><span class="mtag warn">02 · legacy</span><h3>Fix a bug in untested legacy code</h3></header>
      <p>No tests cover the change site. The guard <strong>switches modes</strong> instead of blocking you.</p>
      <ol class="flow">
        <li>systematic-debugging → reproduce &amp; find root cause</li>
        <li>write a <strong>characterization test</strong> that pins current behavior</li>
        <li>change with the safety net — drift becomes a visible diff</li>
        <li>one test around the change site — never a blocked commit</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mfoot mono">// shipped upgrade #6 — legacy-safe test discipline</p>
    </article>

    <article class="mission reveal">
      <header><span class="mtag">03 · parallel</span><h3>Fan out a sprint</h3></header>
      <p>Several independent workstreams. But first: <em>should</em> this even be parallel?</p>
      <ol class="flow">
        <li>the "when NOT to parallelize" gate (~15× token cost check)</li>
        <li>4-layer conflict prevention: paths, worktrees, contracts, deps</li>
        <li>dispatch disjoint agents in one message, isolated worktrees</li>
        <li>serial fan-in: 6-gate each, orchestrator commits in order</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mfoot mono">// shipped upgrade #4 — when-not-to-parallelize</p>
    </article>

    <article class="mission reveal">
      <header><span class="mtag">04 · cost</span><h3>Spend the right model</h3></header>
      <p>Not every task needs the top tier. Routing matches model to judgment density.</p>
      <ol class="flow">
        <li><span class="badge m-opus">opus</span> plans &amp; synthesizes (design, orchestration)</li>
        <li><span class="badge m-sonnet">sonnet</span> implements against the design doc</li>
        <li><span class="badge m-haiku">haiku</span> navigates &amp; does mechanical edits</li>
        <li>escalate only on evidence (≥2 failing-gate rounds)</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mfoot mono">// shipped upgrade #5 — cost-aware routing</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- ===================== NON-NEGOTIABLES ===================== -->
<section class="sheet"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">// flight rules</p>
  <h2>The non-negotiables</h2>
  <ul class="rules">
    <li class="reveal"><b>Design-first (A005)</b> — no code without a merged design doc.</li>
    <li class="reveal"><b>TDD-first (A001)</b> — a failing test before implementation; characterization-first on legacy.</li>
    <li class="reveal"><b>6-gate review (A004)</b> — inspect → build+test → boundary → spec → quality → wiring → smoke.</li>
    <li class="reveal"><b>Live mini-retro (A009)</b> — every task captures a lesson before the next.</li>
    <li class="reveal"><b>Conform to the codebase</b> — match the project's real conventions; never impose an architecture.</li>
  </ul>
</div></section>

<!-- ===================== INSTALL ===================== -->
<section class="sheet soft install" id="install"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">// clearance to install</p>
  <h2>Wheels up in three commands</h2>
  <pre class="terminal reveal"><code><span class="c"># 1 · clone the template</span>
git clone __GH__.git ~/code/claude-flightdeck

<span class="c"># 2 · install into your project (core is architecture-agnostic)</span>
~/code/claude-flightdeck/install.sh ~/code/my-project

<span class="c"># 3 · health check, then open in Claude Code and run /onboard</span>
bash ~/code/my-project/.claude/skills/onboard/scripts/doctor.sh</code></pre>
  <p class="muted">Prereqs: <code>bash</code> + <code>git</code> + <code>jq</code>. Plugins: <code>pr-review-toolkit</code> (required) + <code>superpowers</code> (recommended). Then drive it with <code>/next-task · /post-delegation-gate · /retro · /ratify-rules</code>.</p>
  <div class="cta">
    <a class="btn primary" href="__GH__#quick-start" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Full quick-start ↗</a>
    <a class="btn" href="workflow.html">Understand the workflow →</a>
  </div>
</div></section>
